why did wendy and marty make that tough  decision what did the car crash really  mean what was up with wendy's time in  the mental health hospital here's the  ending of ozark season 4 explained  spoilers ahead  while sam dermody might be gullible we  can all agree that he still deserves a  pleasant send-off throughout the series  the main characters move him wherever  they need him resulting in him working  for ruth at the lazy-o motel a property  she uses to launder money for darlene  and now look at you look you've landed  this great new job worked out better  than i'd hoped sam ultimately escapes  the ozark madness by looking toward a  higher power he's baptized and leaves  town with nathan and the congregation  meaning that he will no longer  unknowingly aid and abet the main  characters in their crimes at least one  character appears to have a happily ever  after at the ending of ozark  in the final hour wendy makes a bold  move by checking herself into a mental  health facility to get her kids back  charlotte and jonah had planned on going  into nathan's custody giving him a  victory albeit short-lived over wendy i  know he's better than mom  jonah what it's not  he is and besides this will be a good  chance to get to know him  credit where credit's due ruth does play  a major role in keeping the four birds  together when she threatens nathan at  gunpoint in his motel room but it's  windy who makes an emotional gambit to  get the kids back on her side when jonah  and charlotte go visit her she redeems  herself by coming clean about her  brother's death it's my fault  all of it  at long last she takes responsibility  for his demise and apologizes to her  kids which is likely all jonah ever  wanted to hear in the end nathan leaves  the ozarks with the rest of the  congregation while jonah and charlotte  stay by their parents  omar spends most of the final season  behind bars and when he's finally  released from jail he's driven to the  middle of nowhere and killed by an  officer  marty proving to be one step ahead of  everyone for the entire series eerily  foreshadowed omar's death when he told  camila that if omar were to be killed  while transferring it would be  considered fate with omar officially out  of the picture the cartel is turned over  to camila omar was supposed to be  released from prison transferred to  mexico and then broken out to head the  cartel once again but camilla is the one  who gets the final deal with the fbi  resulting in omar becoming a little more  than a pawn in the bird's eventual bid  for freedom  season 4 kicks off with the birds  getting in a major car crash however  this scene isn't revisited until the  series finale although it's common for  fans to try to make every single detail  and decision meaningful this accident  feels more like a misdirect rather than  a major plot development the car  accident however does indicate how much  the family has been through as it  doesn't seem to phase them as much as  fans might expect though they're  initially startled they then hop in a  cab head home and seemingly aren't  affected one bit by the accident however  while it doesn't affect the plot much it  does offer the opportunity for  conflicting viewpoints navarro's priest  looks at the accident as a sign of the  birds lives being destructive how many  times does god have to point at you  before you take notice  wendy on the other hand views the event  as proof that her family is going to be  fine they are alive at the end although  jonah has to murder someone to make it  happen so who knows what comes next for  the birds ultimately it may be up to the  audience to decide which meaning is true  sort of a choose your own adventure of  thematic symbolism  camila may have taken over the cartel  but she still doesn't know who killed  javi for just a little while it looks  like things will stay that way until a  big mood change happens at the gala  camilla pressures claire to give up  javi's real killer it was ruth langmore  camilla then threatens to take out the  bird's children if they attempt to warn  ruth in any way and in the end they  choose their own safety over ruth's life  needless to say the ending of ozark is  bittersweet for the birds and audiences  what if this is too much to bear  it won't be  entering the series finale it appears  that ruth just might get away with  javi's murder right up until claire  gives her up to camilla that is this  leads to camilla waiting at ruth's home  and in a shocking scene killing her with  a pull of a trigger ruth's death leaves  three as the sole survivor of the  langmores  though his storyline is left up in the  air  also unknown is what will happen to  ruth's portion of the casino it wouldn't  be surprising if her stakes in the  company go to three or even rachel  garrison who came back to the ozarks to  help run the casino even if rachel  doesn't get it it was a nice surprise  for fans to see her back for the series  finale  in the final scene melsa team shows up  at marty and wendy's house and reveals  that he finally pieced together ben's  murder however just when it seems like  the birds are finally going to go down  for one of their countless crimes jonah  pulls up with a shotgun the scene ends  with a black screen and a gunshot  fan theories will likely run wild with  this ending but it's pretty evident that  jonah pulls the trigger and the birds  get off scot-free so much for going  legit  for most of the series audiences don't  know if the bird family members will  live or die let alone reunite especially  marty as he is consistently put in  harm's way  yet against all odds the birds make a  deal with camilla and the fbi buying  their freedom from the cartel and  immunity from the fbi wendy continuously  says her family is close to making all  their ambitions a reality though it took  several years and many close calls she  is right in the end when season four  ends the family is free to do whatever  they want with the rest of their lives  no longer taking orders from people who  could have them killed with the snap of  a finger  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite shows are coming soon  subscribe to our youtube channel and hit  the bell so you don't miss a single one
 

